%global stage @STAGE@
%global debug_package %{nil}
%global __os_install_post %{nil}
%global __strip /bin/true
%global _build_id_links none
%undefine _missing_build_ids_terminate_build
# The sensor framework records the modification time of every configuration file it parsed in its registry
# (sns_reg_config) and re-parses a file whose mtime differs, discarding the entries first. The payload keeps
# Windows' mtimes, so Fedora's clamping of file times to the changelog date must stay off.
%global source_date_epoch_from_changelog 0
%global clamp_mtime_to_source_date_epoch 0

Name:           sp11-sensors
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        1%{?dist}
Summary:        Surface Pro 11 sensors: Snapdragon Sensor Core configuration, registry and desktop integration
License:        GPL-3.0-or-later AND LicenseRef-Proprietary-Firmware
ExclusiveArch:  aarch64
AutoReqProv:    no

# 0.5.0-3 serves the framework's registry writes, including large ones, and its temporary file next to the registry
Requires:       hexagonrpc >= 0.5.0-3
Requires:       libssc
Requires:       iio-sensor-proxy >= 3.9
Requires:       qrtr
Requires:       systemd
Requires:       systemd-udev
Requires:       policycoreutils
# stdbuf (line-buffered daemon log); dracut for the trigger below, which takes the 1.1/1.2 initramfs hook out
Requires:       coreutils
Requires:       dracut
Requires:       sp11-surface-support >= 2.0

%description
Device-bound sensor support for Microsoft Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100, SKU @SKU@).
The accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer and light sensor hang off the ADSP's
Snapdragon Sensor Core, so this package carries what that framework reads through
hexagonrpcd: the sensor configuration from the Windows driver package (@SNSCFG@),
the registry the framework wrote on this unit's Windows installation (per-sensor
platform data and calibration) and the platform identity files, under
@PAYLOAD_DIR@. It adds the udev and systemd glue that starts the file server when
the ADSP comes up and hands the sensors to iio-sensor-proxy (auto-rotation,
ambient light, compass), a SELinux module for iio-sensor-proxy's QRTR sockets, a
dnf exclusion that keeps the SSC-enabled iio-sensor-proxy, and sp11-sensors-check.
The configuration and registry files are Microsoft/Qualcomm proprietary and must
not be redistributed. Reboot after installing: the framework reads the registry
only when the ADSP boots.
Inputs: @INPUTS@

%prep
%build

%install
cp -a %{stage}/. %{buildroot}/

%post
# systemd's RPM file triggers reload the units and udev rules. The policy module is what lets iio-sensor-proxy
# open QRTR sockets under enforcing; a system without a policy store has nothing to load into.
if [ -d /etc/selinux/targeted ] && [ -x /usr/sbin/semodule ]; then
  /usr/sbin/semodule -i /usr/share/selinux/packages/sp11-sensors.cil >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
fi
%systemd_post sp11-sensors-resume.service
%posttrans
# The working directory the daemon serves (links into the package plus a writable copy of the registry under
# sensors/persist): made here and not in %%post, because on an upgrade %%post runs while the previous release's
# payload files are still in place and the copy would take them along (seen with 1.4's sns_reg_version). 1.3 and
# 1.4 kept the copy at sensors/registry, which nothing serves any more.
rm -rf /var/lib/sp11/hexagonrpc/sensors/registry
/usr/bin/systemd-tmpfiles --create /usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/sp11-sensors.conf >/dev/null 2>&1 || :

# 1.1 and 1.2 put an initramfs hook (95sp11-sensors) into the running kernel's initramfs, an early attach the
# framework turned out not to need; regenerating the initramfs when one of them is upgraded away takes the hook
# out. Up to 1.9 this ran in %%posttrans on every install: a full host-only dracut each time, for nothing. Nothing
# to do in a live session or a build chroot.
%triggerpostun -- sp11-sensors < 1.3
if [ -f "/boot/initramfs-$(uname -r).img" ] && ! grep -qw rd.live.image /proc/cmdline 2>/dev/null; then
  /usr/bin/dracut -f --kver "$(uname -r)" >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
fi

%preun
%systemd_preun sp11-sensors-online.service sp11-sensors-resume.service

%postun
if [ $1 -eq 0 ]; then
  [ -x /usr/sbin/semodule ] && /usr/sbin/semodule -r sp11-sensors >/dev/null 2>&1 || :
  rm -rf /var/lib/sp11/hexagonrpc
fi

%files
%defattr(-,root,root,-)
@PAYLOAD_DIR@/
/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/81-sp11-sensors.rules
%dir /usr/lib/systemd/system/hexagonrpcd-adsp-sensorspd.service.d
/usr/lib/systemd/system/hexagonrpcd-adsp-sensorspd.service.d/10-sp11.conf
/usr/lib/systemd/system/sp11-sensors-online.service
/usr/lib/systemd/system/sp11-sensors-resume.service
/usr/lib/systemd/system/suspend.target.wants/sp11-sensors-resume.service
/usr/lib/systemd/system/suspend-then-hibernate.target.wants/sp11-sensors-resume.service
/usr/libexec/sp11/sp11-sensors-wait
/usr/libexec/sp11/sp11-sensors-check
/usr/libexec/sp11/sp11-sensors-guard
/usr/libexec/sp11/sp11-sensors-reset
/usr/lib/tmpfiles.d/sp11-sensors.conf
/usr/share/selinux/packages/sp11-sensors.cil
/etc/dnf/libdnf5.conf.d/91-sp11-sensors.conf

%changelog
* Tue Sep 22 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - @VERSION@-1
- The initramfs is regenerated only when a 1.1 or 1.2 package (the initramfs hook) is upgraded away, by a
  trigger, not on every install; sp11-sensors-reset says the rebuilt registry copy is read at the next boot;
  comments in the daemon drop-in, the check and wait helpers match the current design (registry read once per
  ADSP boot, POS tablet switch); the payload's inputs hash in the description (step 45 refuses a same-version
  rebuild from other inputs)

* Mon Sep 21 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.9-1
- sp11-sensors-wait no longer restarts iio-sensor-proxy: a sensor type the proxy lacks (usually the compass,
  published after its probe) is picked up by sending the proxy a udev "add" event for the FastRPC node, repeated
  with a growing delay; the CDSP firmware had asserted during both boot-time restarts seen, while the proxy tore
  its sensor streams down
- sp11-sensors-check: the daemon's memory broken down (cgroup memory.stat, process status and mappings, the DSP's
  memory map requests)

* Mon Sep 21 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.8-1
- sp11-sensors-wait also waits for the compass (libssc's rotation-vector sensor, which comes up after the
  physical sensors) and restarts iio-sensor-proxy when it lacks the accelerometer, the light sensor or the
  compass; the proxy's single probe at boot had found no compass on two of three boots

* Sun Sep 20 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.7-1
- sp11-sensors-check: a "tablet mode" section (switch input devices, Surface Aggregator modules and kernel
  lines, libinput capabilities, iio-sensor-proxy's HasAccelerometer, mutter's PanelOrientationManaged, connected
  Bluetooth devices) for the missing auto-rotate toggle; the DSP's write activity summarised instead of buried in
  the log's head and tail; "files the DSP wrote" measured against the attach marker (same clock domain)

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.6-1
- sns_reg_version and parsed_file_list.csv beside the registry copy (sensors/persist), where Windows keeps them
  and where the framework looks for them (served among the entries, it deleted them and tried to create
  sns_reg_version); the payload carries them in sensors/registry-parent

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.5-1
- Writable parent for the registry (sensors/persist, the framework's temporary file lands there), configuration
  files keep Windows' modification times (the framework re-parses a file whose mtime differs from the stamp in
  its registry), accelerometer mount matrix for iio-sensor-proxy, no proxy restart when it already has the
  sensors, crash counts per remote processor in sp11-sensors-check; needs hexagonrpc 0.5.0-3 (large writes)

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.4-1
- The guard runs as ExecCondition: its refusal skips the unit instead of failing it, so Restart= never re-runs
  it (RestartPreventExitStatus= applies to the main process only; an ExecStartPre failure was restarted up to
  the start limit)

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.3-1
- Writable registry copy under /var/lib/sp11/hexagonrpc (tmpfiles), crash guard on the unit, no initramfs
  hook, sp11-sensors-reset; needs hexagonrpc 0.5.0-2 (registry writes)

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.2-1
- LF line endings for sns_reg_config, json.lst and the platform files (the DSP kept Windows' CR in the paths it
  parsed and never found its registry); the initramfs hook re-attaches until the sensors PD accepts it

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.1-1
- Attach hexagonrpcd from the initramfs (dracut module), where the ADSP boots; line-buffered daemon log;
  readiness probe through libssc instead of the QMI service list

* Sat Sep 19 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - 1.0-1
- Surface Pro 11 sensors payload and integration
